cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TransitBench, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TransitBench: Can AI agents automate the search for exoplanets?"
abstract: >-
  TransitBench is a benchmark for autonomous scientific programming in
  astronomy. A coding agent gets one year of real Kepler light curves for 196
  labelled dev stars and a weak starter search, and builds a planet-search
  pipeline in Python. When the session ends, the pipeline is frozen and runs
  once, with no language model, on 2,000 hidden stars, where it is scored on
  injected planets found minus false candidates on eclipsing binaries and
  Kepler false alarms.
authors:
